 "about": "Liquid thermal conductivity calculated from the correlation of Perkins and Huber (2011, eqs 2-4, Tables 1-2), which they fitted to their measurements (transient hot wire, 302-508 K, uncertainty below 1 %); at 101.325 kPa, with the liquid density of the equation of state of Huber et al. (2009) as implemented in CoolProp 8.0.0, the one the authors used; without the critical enhancement, negligible below 500 K as the article states. 'uncertainty' is the 2.5 % (95 % confidence) the authors give for the correlation. Written by validation/python/perkins2011_conductivity.py, which first reproduces the check values of the article's Table 3. The measured values themselves are in the article's supporting information, not used here.",
